A||||6||voyagerspe||V8: Alternative to Moroso oil block off plate||||3||
Z||000000||voyagerspe||10-23-2001||12:07 AM||||I didnt like the Moroso block off plate for the oil filter relocation (I got 2 bad ones (cracks)) So we came up with this; Im sure its been done before but since I had some good pics I thought I would share.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-007S_2.JPG">  <P>First we used a tap to put some 3/8 pipe thread into the block  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-008S_3.JPG[/img" TARGET=_blank>]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-008S_3.JPG[/img]</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-009S_3.JPG[/img" TARGET=_blank>]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-009S_3.JPG[/img]</A> <BR>Then we drilled the outer hole (where the oil sending unit would go ) so that that we could <BR>pass the tap through the outer hole and tap the inner hole to put in 3/8 pipe thread <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-010S.JPG[/img" TARGET=_blank>]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-010S.JPG[/img]</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-011S_2.JPG[/img" TARGET=_blank>]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-011S_2.JPG[/img]</A> <P>Then I added some 3/8 black pipe<BR> [URL=http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-014S_2.JPG[/img<P><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-014S_2.JPG[/img][/URL]" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-014S_2.JPG[/img][/URL]</A>  <P>All done: no leaks<P> <P>[This message has been edited by voyagerspe (edited 10-23-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by voyagerspe (edited 10-23-2001).]||||reg||3
